<title>USA: Alabama jobless rate up slightly in September.</title>
<headline>Alabama jobless rate up slightly in September.</headline>
<dateline>MONTGOMERY, Ala 1996-10-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Alabama's unemployment rate rose to 4.7 percent in September from 4.5 percent in August and 6.5 percent a year ago, the state Department of Industrial Relations said.</p>
<p>The September figure was still the lowest for that month in 22 years, department Director Dottie Cieszynski said. The figure represents 98,300 unemployed residents, compared to 94,100 in August and 133,800 in September 1995.</p>
<p>Alabama gained 1,100 manufacturing jobs in September but that was more than offset by job losses in services and government sectors.</p>
<p>--Jane Sutton, 305-374-5013</p>
</text>
